# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undal customer website — Cloudflare Pages redirects
#
# One address per page. The build appends a rule for every snapshot it writes
# (`/store/index.html` → `/store`), and `web/src/serve.ts` redirects the same
# shapes for any path the Function serves, so this file is the belt to that
# brace: a `public/` directory hosted anywhere else still has one canonical URL
# per page, and a crawler that guesses `index.html` is told where the real one is
# instead of being shown the same menu twice.
#
# Nothing here redirects a POST. Undal's no-JavaScript ordering path posts to
# /basket/add and /checkout/place, and a 301 is allowed to drop the body of a
# POST — a customer's basket is not something to gamble on a status code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/index.html  /  301
